# sys.allow - the census allow list of sysfail_fuzzer's system-call schedule (build.sh, OV_DSL_ALLOW).
#
# oss-verify's dsl.py renames lib/liboft.a's copy with sysfail_fuzzer.tramp_alloc.redefs and
# sysfail_fuzzer.tramp_sys.redefs, and then accepts each name that the copy still leaves undefined only when the
# copy defines it, it is a new name of a map, it starts with __asan_, __ubsan_, __sanitizer_, __start_ or
# __stop_, or it is a line of this file (docs/build-contract.md, "DSL fuzz targets"). These are the C library
# functions that zlib 1.4 calls at the pinned commit; none of them makes a file system call, so none can touch a
# file outside the schedule. malloc is not here because the allocation map renames it (tramp_malloc); free allocates
# nothing and is not scheduled (sysfail_fuzzer.tramp_alloc.redefs). strerror formats zlib's error messages from
# errno; musl's makes no system call. A new name here must be argued the same way: one that can reach the kernel
# belongs in a rename map, not in this list.
__errno_location
free
memchr
memcpy
memmove
memset
snprintf
strerror
strlen
vsnprintf
